# Review routing. Agent commits are marked by their trailers; these rules make sure
# that a PR touching a path the agent gate guards, or a server-only module, asks
# the owner for review. GitHub only BLOCKS on it once branch protection turns on
# "Require review from Code Owners" for master (see docs/AI_HARNESS.md "Provenance").
#
# Supported forms (src/lib/codeownersCoverage.test.ts holds the file to them):
#   /dir/        a directory, anchored at the repo root
#   /file        one file, anchored at the repo root
#   *.ext        every file with that extension
# Every anchored path must exist, and every path the gate protects must be owned.

# Repo law, the agent contract, CI and the gate scripts
/.claude/ @xkazm04
/.ai/ @xkazm04
/.github/ @xkazm04
/scripts/ @xkazm04

